THIS LICENCE COVERS ALOUD'S OWN SOURCE CODE ONLY. IT DOES NOT COVER THE MODEL.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Aloud speaks using the Supertonic 3 model, and that model's *weights* are NOT
MIT. They are released under the BigScience Open RAIL-M License, which carries
use restrictions that MIT does not — see LICENSES/supertonic-weights-OpenRAIL-M.txt.
The weights are not contained in this repository; they are downloaded at
runtime. Conflating the two licences is the specific mistake this note exists to
prevent, and hard constraint 3 in CLAUDE.md says so at more length.

Third-party components are listed in LICENSES/. That directory is NOT yet a
complete third-party notice for the compiled binary: Aloud statically links a
large Rust dependency tree plus ONNX Runtime, and no generated NOTICE exists
yet. That obligation bites on distribution, not on building locally.
